From 6b73cc9a1cb39a97b070543dcc352ca627581642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:57:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: add MT7987 WED v3.1 support

Port the WED v3.1 and RRO v3.1 interface from MediaTek SDK 25.12
fb7d0538 onto mt76 0936617d. Keep the upstream TX-free completion,
WED v2 RX drop and RRO v3 RX queuing fixes already in this baseline.

Configure the dedicated WED-to-host RX ring and include it in the
NAPI interrupt mask and recovery path. Adapt mt7915 and mt7996 to
per-queue WPDMA TX addresses, and select RRO mode by WED version.
Do not attempt a secondary WED attach when the primary attach failed.

For MT7987 only, keep WED tokens in [0, 16384) and host tokens in
[16384, 31744), avoiding the TX-free token collision that stalls ALTX
and beacons. Preserve the existing host token capacity and WED buffer
budget on other platforms. Remember the per-device capacity across
flow offload disable/enable, and count only tokens inside the WED
range when draining host-owned tokens.

Based on MediaTek SDK commits b611161a6bcca27618c332e8f0ecffbcd30fea30,
3365d5a99e648a51a638d68c384005765cd7a8c7,
303f415b6a793123f8ee5e176abef4f80de3ff7c,
fcea34c9147e46118d215c374233c1034ce05ab9,
ba05806b7f5f922f8e7cfa07a8f8eb7d368e2fc8 and
704b6b27c109f19db03428d2f43e4305f2f87a73 by Rex Lu
<rex.lu@mediatek.com>, Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com> and
Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>, with the WPDMA array and
host token corrections by huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>.

Keep the WED v3.1 capability check available when WED is disabled.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
